.TH LLM-MANAGER-RESTORE-SETUP 8 "2026-09-06" "LLM-Manager"
.SH NAME
llm-manager-restore-setup \- explicitly initialize local root backup storage
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B llm-manager-restore-setup initialize
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run explicitly as an administrator with effective UID 0.
Creates only fixed root-owned private directories beneath
/var/lib/llm-manager/local-root-restore and a random local-root-v1 key.
No password, key content, key name, or pathname is accepted as input.
There is no automatic setup during installation, Apply, review, or restore.
.PP
Existing keys, backups, history, unexpected entries, and interrupted key
publication cause refusal. No rotation, replacement, repair, or deletion is
performed. Retain existing evidence and seek administrator review on failure.
An incomplete directory-only initialization can be retried while all state
directories are empty and their ownership and permissions remain valid.
.PP
This entry is administrator-only and has no PolicyKit action or GUI launcher.
Initializing storage does not enable the normal GUI root route.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 indicates initialization completed; 1 indicates rejection or an incomplete
operation. Output is bounded metadata JSON and never includes key bytes.
.SH SEE ALSO
llm-manager-helper(8), llm-manager-restore-review(8), llm-manager-restore-execute(8)
